ise with it, and in time many became full members, while one who resisted or fled could be killed.","why":"The mourning wars brought captives into the villages to replace the dead.","people":[["pierre-esprit-radisson","Pierre-Esprit Radisson"]]},{"n":8,"lv":5,"band":"enslaved","name":"Captives kept as slaves","loc":"Gatsennen","term":"","lbl":"c. 0.5–2% (est.)","w":1.25,"firm":1,"est":1,"pic":"/images/societies/thumbs/haudenosaunee-8.jpg","you":"You were taken in a raid and not adopted: you work at the village’s tasks, may be traded away, and the word for you is the word for a domestic animal.","kid":"Some captives were not adopted and had to work for the village, or were traded away.","rise":"War, ransom or a family’s choice put a captive here; adoption was the way out, and a captive who resisted could be killed. Once European settlers brought African slavery to North America, some Haudenosaunee, such as Joseph Brant, owned enslaved Africans.","why":"Not every captive was adopted.","people":[]}]}</script>
